You are the PM running three workstreams (V1, V2, V3) from the exo performance campaign. A researcher already delivered the analysis; your job is EXECUTION of the zero-cluster-cost parts plus preparation of the one profiling run that needs user approval. Work autonomously through phases; only stop early for a genuine blocker.

## Read first

1. /Users/adam.durham/.hermes/cache/research-findings-v1v2v3.md - the full findings, hypotheses, evidence citations, and experiment sketches. AUTHORITATIVE.
2. /Users/adam.durham/repos/exo/docs/PERFORMANCE_HISTORY.md - the master campaign doc (~7600 lines). Search for: "P15 RESULT", "P12 RESULT", "DEFECT", "DEPLOY", "P13 pre-register", "P06 Phase C", "SPEC_STATE_RESTORE", "rb_snap".

## Hard constraints (violating any is a fail)

1. NO cluster relaunches, NO process kills, NO config changes on the nodes, NO production writes. Read-only analysis + writing scratch files only.
2. NO boot experiments. NO new benchmark runs against the live cluster.
3. V4 (c=2 concurrency) is DROPPED by user decision. Do not pursue, do not plan.
4. Root-cause framing only. No mitigations.
5. Do NOT re-propose NOT-FUNDED items (further head sharding, rowseq-GEMM custom kernels, tree drafting, context caps).
6. Do NOT commit or push anything. All artifacts go under /Users/adam.durham/repos/exo/tmp/research-v1v2v3-20260901/ (create it). The supervisor commits later.
7. Read-only ssh to the nodes (adams-mac-studio-m4-1.local, adams-mac-studio-m4-2.local) is allowed for log inspection ONLY. Never run anything that modifies state there.

## Phases

### Phase 0 - V2 feasibility check (~10 min, do FIRST)
Check whether server-side per-cycle acceptance counters exist in node logs for the P11-P15 window (Aug 31). Inspect ~/.exo/exo_log/ on both nodes: rotated zst files (use zstdcat if available, else python3 -c with zstandard) and live exo.log. Look for per-cycle MTP lines ([MTP], acceptance counters, "accepted", mtp_cycle_time.py-compatible lines). ALSO check whether bench/mtp_cycle_time.py exists in the repo and what exact format it parses. Report feasibility verdict.

### If feasible: run V2 fully
Parse acceptance counters for the Aug 31 boots, join to per-rep decode JSONs (tmp/p13-relaunch-20260831/, tmp/p14-armA-20260831/, tmp/p14-armB-20260831/, tmp/p15-replication-20260831/, and P06/P11/P12 if data exists), regress per-rep decode_tps on per-rep mean acceptance within and across boots. Apply the pre-registered bands from the findings file (>50% explained -> mechanism named; <20% -> verify-cost side).

### If not feasible
Document exactly what is missing, then proceed.

## Phase V1 - zero-cost part + telemetry kit

1. Extend the warmup analysis if new data found in V2 mining.
2. Grep node logs (read-only) for the P13/P14/P15 boot windows: Metal/IOGPU warnings, Jetsam/memory-pressure events, runner-restart events (PID+lstart forensics). Report what exists.
3. Write the passive telemetry kit: a script (Python or bash) that samples, per node: mx.metal active memory + allocator cache size (via mlx python), powermetrics GPU clocks/residency/power (sudo -n powermetrics is NOPASSWD per sudoers), memory_pressure, wired limit, runner PID+lstart. Designed to run at T0/warmup/after-each-rep during a future launch. Test the script's read-only parts locally where possible. Do NOT execute it on the cluster.

## Phase V3 - prepare only, do NOT relaunch

1. Verify the rb_snap profiling bracket exists at dsv4_mtp.py:4111-4145 (read the code; confirm EXO_DSV4_MTP_PROFILE and EXO_DSV4_RB_PROFILE env gates).
2. Confirm save_meta behavior at cache.py:2533-2568 and the per-cycle call site at dsv4_mtp.py:4118-4128 (read, cite line numbers).
3. Write the exact profiling-run plan: env vars to set in start_cluster.sh invocation (EXO_DSV4_MTP_PROFILE, EXO_DSV4_RB_PROFILE, plus any needed), what to measure, how many reps, the pre-registered gate (rb_snap >= 3-5% of cycle time -> proceed; <1ms -> close), and which artifacts to collect. This run REQUIRES a cluster relaunch and therefore REQUIRES user approval - you must NOT execute it. Deliver it as an execution-ready plan.

## Deliverable

Write a final report to /Users/adam.durham/repos/exo/tmp/research-v1v2v3-20260901/REPORT.md containing:
- V2 feasibility verdict + results (or why not)
- V1 log-mining findings
- V3 profiling-run plan (execution-ready, with exact commands and env vars)
- Any blockers

Do NOT commit anything. Report back a summary: what was found, what is ready, and the exact one action that needs user approval (the profiled relaunch).
