ll replicated to 0.02% while decode swung 16.7% — since prefill and decode share the same process/config/hardware, a real code bug would move both, not just one. The original static-code analysis (both flags individually inert at decode's actual shape) was right from the start; the \"interaction effect\" theory built across P13/Arm A/Arm B was a lucky-boot artifact, not a real finding, and the investigation correctly let its own replication attempt overturn that conclusion rather than rationalizing around a contradicting result.\n\nTwo good things came out of this anyway: a genuine, independent, pre-existing bug (`BatchPoolingCache` overlap-carry lists not resizing on batch-width change — dated back to 2026-08-20, unrelated to tonight's work) was found and root-caused as a side effect, and there's now a documented methodological rule for the rest of this campaign: don't trust a single-boot decode delta smaller than ~6 tok/s.\n\n**Net effect on tonight's actual shipped work**: nothing changes. P08 and P09's prefill wins are untouched and confirmed real (prefill is boot-stable), both flags correctly stay on, and production is healthy on exactly the intended shipped configuration.", "timestamp": 1788239511.6152902}, {"id": 333178, "role": "user", "content": "[ASYNC DELEGATION BATCH COMPLETE — deleg_1c395a3a]\nA background fan-out of 1 subagent(s) you dispatched earlier has finished. All ran in parallel and waited on each other; their consolidated results are below. You may have moved on since dispatching — act on these or re-dispatch if things have changed.\n\nDispatched: 2026-08-31 20:36:02 (3h37m ago)\nContext you provided: REPO: ~/repos/exo (main branch), submodule ~/repos/exo/mlx-lm. HEAD == origin/main at 91bfa9122 (P12 result committed: decode regression confirmed real, survives a cold relaunch, -6.13% vs P06 reference at median 32.18 tok/s vs 34.28; both named candidate flags EXO_DSV4_QUERY_TILED_SDPA and EXO_DSV4_EXACT_TOPK_PREFILL independently verified via st