t. This exact class of bug (a knob not reaching the live process) has invalidated 4 separate measurements this campaign already.\n3. Run the identical probe: 100K depth, --max-tokens 1200, warmup + n=3 sequential reps, decode_sample_trustworthy=true required on all 3.\n4. Score against the pre-registered gates VERBATIM from the doc, do not paraphrase or round differently, do not rationalize a near-miss:\n   - CONFIG-IMPLICATED: median >= 33.25 tok/s → the two flags DO cause the loss despite the static analysis; the static analysis is WRONG and must be reopened at the kernel level. Next step: single-flag split to isolate which one.\n   - CONFIG-EXONERATED: median < 33.25 tok/s → the flags are not the cause; the static traces are corroborated. Next step is a code-level bisect of the mlx-lm submodule pointer diff (a6eb893->2e2d17d) OUTSIDE the two gated paths already checked, NOT further flag A/Bs.\n   - AMBIGUOUS: median lands 32.89-33.25 with reps straddling → escalate to n=5 before concluding anything.\n5. Also worth a quick look, flagged in the pre-registration: P12's within-run spread (31.36-32.89, range 1.53) was much wider than P06's (34.12-34.35, range 0.23) -- if P13 also comes back wide, between-boot probe reproducibility is itself an unmeasured variable worth a note, thou…", "timestamp": 1788239641.773126, "anchor": true, "content_truncated": true, "original_content_chars": 11132}, {"id": 333179, "role": "assistant", "content": "Let me do a final independent verification pass on the pieces I haven't already directly checked — particularly the new fix commit and final cluster state, since PIDs have changed again since my last check.", "timestamp": 1788239657.368656, "tool_calls": [{"id": "toolu_013xzyAcQMxWr9pBUzjYMxDK", "call_id": "toolu_013xzyAcQMxWr9pBUzjYMxDK", "response_item_id": "fc_toolu_013xzyAcQMxWr9pBUzjYMxDK", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "terminal", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd ~/repos/exo && echo \\\"=== git state ===\\\" && git l